@startuml egress-decision
' UML activity diagram: the grant at run start, then one decision per connection.
' Source of record for docs/diagrams/egress-decision.svg. Do not edit the SVG:
' render it with the pinned PlantUML image (docs/adopting.md).
' &#45;&#45; is a literal "--": PlantUML reads --text-- as strikeout.
title The egress decision: grant at start, checked answer per connection

start
:read the profile's network.egress\nand the class allowlist gateway/classes/<class>.toml;
if (a profile destination is outside the class?) then (yes)
  :refuse before anything starts:\nthe class is a ceiling the profile cannot raise;
  stop
endif
:grant = profile egress ∩ class allowlist,\nwith the class's wildcard and port matching;
if (grant empty?) then (yes)
  :announce "egress grant is empty: this jail has no route out"\n(started, not refused);
endif
:start the gateway with &#45;&#45;grant <host:port,…>;
:CONNECT host:port from the jail;
if (host is an IP literal?) then (yes)
  :deny reason=ip-literal;
  stop
endif
switch (host:port against the grant)
case (in the grant)
  :resolve the name once;
  :check every answer against the blocked ranges;
  if (an answer is blocked?) then (yes)
    :deny reason=blocked-<range>,\nno address is tried;
    stop
  endif
  :connect to the pinned address,\nno re-resolution, no unchecked fallback;
  :audit allow with resolved=… pinned=…;
case (in the class, not in the profile grant)
  :deny reason=not-in-profile;
  stop
case (not in the class either)
  :deny reason=not-in-class;
  stop
endswitch
stop
legend bottom
  The DNS half makes the same decision in one step: a granted name answers
  127.0.0.1, and any other name is nxdomain with reason not-in-profile (the
  class has it, this jail was not granted it) or not-in-class.
endlegend
@enduml
